1.3  Aims and learning outcomes

Our Cambridge National in Engineering Design will
encourage students to:

•	 understand and apply the fundamental principles
and concepts of Engineering Design, including
the design process, types of drawings, influences
on design, and the use of Computer Aided Design
(CAD)

•	 develop learning and practical skills that can be
applied to real-life contexts and work situations

•

think creatively, innovatively, analytically, logically
and critically

•	 develop independence and confidence in using
skills that would be relevant to the engineering
design and development sector and more widely

•	 analyse problems in design terms through practical
experience of solving such problems, including
designing, and modelling designs to meet a design
brief

•	 understand the different stages of the iterative

design process, recognising the cyclical nature of
this approach

•	 evaluate designs through product disassembly and

the process of using product analysis.

