4.4  Unit R040: Design, evaluation and modelling

Aims

Designers need an understanding of how products
are manufactured to ensure that their ideas can be
produced effectively.  Analysing how products are
made can help to inform designs, and it can be useful
to disassemble existing products to discover how they
function and how they were manufactured.

You will develop your virtual modelling skills using
computer aided design (CAD) 3D software, to produce
a high-quality model that will be able to simulate your
design prototype. You will also develop your physical
modelling skills using modelling materials or rapid-
prototyping processes to produce a physical prototype.

