Inconsistencies throughout a student’s response are
often indicators of plagiarism. For example:

•	 dated expressions and references to past events as

being current

•	 different tones of voice, sentence structure and

•

formality across pieces of work

sections of text in a document where the font or
format is inconsistent with other sections.

•	 use of American expressions, spellings and contexts

(such as American laws and guidelines)

What to do if you think a student has plagiarised

If you identify plagiarised work at the point of marking
or moderation:

•

•

this must be taken into account when applying the
