What improper assistance might look like

When we see anything that suggests the teacher has
led students to the answer, we become concerned
because it suggests students have not worked
independently to produce their assignment work. The
following are examples of what may indicate improper
assistance by the teacher:

•	 prompts that instruct students to include specific

detail in their work, such as, ‘You need to define the
difference between sketching techniques. How are
they used? Which techniques are most appropriate?’

•	 headings or templates that include examples which
give all or part of what students have to write about
or produce, such as planning the manufacture of a
prototype.

